{
  "case_id": "2020-19-546",
  "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Michael R. Huston)",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. HUSTON: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: The text of the FTCA judgment bar resolves this case. The district court entered the judgment in an action under Section 1346(b), so that judgment constitutes a complete bar to any action by Respondent against the federal employees involved in his FTCA claim. That broad text unambiguously precludes Respondent's Bivens action here, which asserts the same injuries based on the very same subject matter."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Huston",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Because the purpose of the judgment bar, Your Honor, is repose. Congress wanted the judgment in the FTCA action to bring repose to the entire controversy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Huston",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think it's possible, Your Honor, because it would be consistent with the goal of the judgment bar to wrap the entire resolution of the claim into the judgment on the FTCA action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: If we do resolve that question, I'm going to reiterate questions asked by others now, but the key problem for you is it says \"any action,\" not \"any claims.\" Do you just want to summarize your best arguments in response to that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jaicomo",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, the judgment bar does not apply to claims brought together in a single action."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Well, I have one unrelated question, brief question. Should it matter in deciding this case that Bivens was -- didn't exist at the time the judgment bar was enacted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE ALITO",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If a district court rejects a claim under the FTCA for failure to proof -- failure of proof, does the judgment bar apply to that, or is that a jurisdictional determination?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0002-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the government requested and received a 12(b)(1) dismissal"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE BARRETT",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what about if it's a summary judgment? Didn't the government also in this case request summary judgment in the alternative?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Embedded in Congress's enactment of the FTCA and its judgment bar, it is a very simple common law doctrine that has been with litigants since the beginning of this country, which is the concept of res judicata."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It should not now be allowed to come to this Court and say: Jurisdiction and merits are the same and -- and merits should, therefore, prevail because, as Wright and Miller in the First Restatement and many other places have said, anytime jurisdiction's entwined with merits, jurisdiction controls, not merits."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "created just such an action by pleading a demand for relief alleging the elements of Section 1346(b), and the district court indisputably entered judgment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Sixth Circuit",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Sixth Circuit explained at Petition Appendix 1A, Note 1, why the district court's judgment is best understood as a summary judgment in favor of the government, because both parties submitted a body of extensive evidentiary exhibits in support of the motion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Now, regarding my friend's fallback argument, I think, as the Court has recognized this morning, it certainly has discretion not to consider that argument in this case, and that's the most appropriate disposition because the alternative question simply isn't cert-worthy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0003-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the 70 years since the judgment bar was enacted, the courts of appeals have overwhelmingly rejected this argument, and that's because, as Justice Breyer recognized, it directly conflicts with Congress's purpose."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2020-19-546",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c885f4756b56460eac53d19ff3637bc994e9a8ad34f90eb8ee1d9a4eb8fec078",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c885f4756b56-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
    {
